D = {
"Balance and Ruin|BMT": "A 100 by 50 foot room has a beam over a 25-foot gear pit. A plate under the beam's near end magnetizes the metal walls. **Tilt.** DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) spots the fulcrum. **Beam.** Difficult terrain. Ending a turn on it or being on it when it tilts needs a DC 12 Dexterity save, with disadvantage in metal while magnetized. Failing by 4 or less means prone. By 5 or more means falling in. **Walls.** Metal-clad creatures off the beam stick, take 11 (2d10) bludgeoning damage, and are restrained until the plate is released. **Pit.** Falling in or ending a turn there needs a DC 17 Dexterity save or 55 (10d10) bludgeoning damage and prone.",
"Bear Trap|XGE": "Iron jaws spiked into the ground snap shut on the leg of whoever steps on them. The victim is immobilized.",
"Collapsing Roof|DMG": "A trip wire 3 inches off the ground between two support beams brings down an unstable ceiling. Spotting the wire is DC 10. A DC 15 Dexterity check with thieves' tools disarms it. Without the tools, use an edged weapon or tool with disadvantage. Failure triggers the trap. A creature can also use an action to knock over a beam and trigger it. Each creature under the section makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 22 (4d10) bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. Rubble then makes the area difficult terrain.",
"Collapsing Roof|XDMG": "A trip wire 3 inches off the ground topples weak supports and collapses a ceiling section. The first creature to cross it triggers the collapse. Each creature beneath makes a DC 13 Dexterity save, taking 11 (2d10) bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. Rubble becomes difficult terrain. **Detect and Disarm.** A Search action and a DC 11 Wisdom (Perception) check finds the wire and the weak ceiling. Then the wire can be cut or avoided freely. **Higher Levels.** Levels 5 to 10: 22 (4d10), DC 15. Levels 11 to 16: 55 (10d10), DC 17. Levels 17 to 20: 99 (18d10), DC 19.",
"Crossbow Trap|XGE": "Kobolds and similar creatures favor this trap. A trip wire across a hallway links to two hidden heavy crossbows aimed down the hall. Disturbing the wire fires them at whoever is there.",
"Danse Macabre|VRGR": "A haunted trap fills a 20-foot-radius sphere around an ancient instrument. Entering the area brings distant mournful music. One round later a phantom performer plays for 1 minute. A creature entering or starting its turn in the area makes a DC 14 Wisdom save or floats 20 feet up and dances as under Otto's irresistible dance. As an action, a dancer can repeat the save to end it, then falls 20 feet and takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage. A successful save grants immunity for 24 hours. A creature can use an action for a DC 14 Charisma (Persuasion) check to make the performer stop. When it stops, everyone floats safely down and is freed.",
"Faceless Malice|VRGR": "A haunted trap covers a 15-foot cube before an ornate wall mirror. A visible creature entering sees its distorted reflection. If it is still there at the start of its next turn, it makes a DC 12 Wisdom save or is blinded, deafened, and unable to speak for 1 minute, and appears to have no face. Remove curse ends the effect, as does destroying the mirror. The mirror has AC 12, 10 hit points, vulnerability to bludgeoning damage, and immunity to poison and psychic damage. After a failed save, the trap stays dormant for 24 hours.",
"Falling Net|DMG": "A trip wire 3 inches off the ground between two columns or trees drops a hidden net. Spotting the wire and net is DC 10. A DC 15 Dexterity check with thieves' tools breaks the wire safely. Without the tools, use an edged weapon or tool with disadvantage. Failure triggers the trap. The net covers a 10-foot square. Creatures under it are restrained, and those failing a DC 10 Strength save are also prone. An action and a DC 10 Strength check frees a creature within reach. The net has AC 10 and 20 hit points. Dealing 5 slashing damage destroys a 5-foot section and frees whoever is in it.",
"Falling Net|XDMG": "A trip wire 3 inches off the ground drops a weighted 10-foot-square Net. The first creature crossing makes a DC 10 Dexterity save or is restrained until it escapes. Huge or larger creatures succeed automatically. An action and DC 10 Strength (Athletics) frees a creature within reach. **Detect and Disarm.** A Search action and DC 11 Wisdom (Perception) finds wire and Net. Then the wire can be cut or avoided freely. **Destroy.** Reducing the Net to 0 hit points frees everyone. **Set.** With Thieves' Tools and a Net, DC 13 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) over 10 minutes. **Higher Levels.** Save and Strength DC: 12 at levels 5 to 10, 14 at 11 to 16, 16 at 17 to 20.",
"Falling Portcullis|XGE": "A pressure plate drops a portcullis far from the plate, often sealing the distant dungeon entrance. Intruders do not know they are trapped until they try to leave. Mad wizards and other builders use it to stop easy escapes.",
"Fiery Blast Trap|XGE": "Stepping on the mosaic makes fire erupt from it. Creatures openly wearing holy symbols of Pyremius do not trigger it.",
"Fire-Breathing Statue|DMG": "A hidden pressure plate makes a nearby statue release a magical 30-foot cone of fire. The plate and faint scorch marks are DC 15 to spot. Detect magic shows an evocation aura on the statue. More than 20 pounds on the plate triggers it. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 13 Dexterity save, taking 22 (4d10) fire damage on a failure or half on a success. Wedging an iron spike or other object under the plate prevents activation. A successful dispel magic (DC 13) on the statue destroys the trap.",
"Fire-Casting Statue|XDMG": "When a creature first moves onto the plate on a turn or starts its turn there, a statue breathes a 15-foot Cone of flame. Each creature makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 11 (2d10) fire damage on a failure or half on a success. **Detect and Disarm.** Detect Magic shows Evocation. A Search action within 5 feet and DC 10 Wisdom (Perception) finds a glyph. Study and DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana) reads it as fire. Defacing it as an action disarms the trap. Search and DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) finds the plate. Iron Spikes under it stop it. **Higher Levels.** Levels 5 to 10: 22 (4d10), 30-foot. 11 to 16: 55 (10d10), 60-foot. 17 to 20: 99 (18d10), 120-foot.",
"Hidden Pit|XDMG": "A 10-foot-deep pit has a hinged lid matching the floor. A creature stepping on it falls in, and the lid stays open. The fall deals 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage. **Detect and Disarm.** A Study action and DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) finds the pit. Wedging an Iron Spike under the lid keeps it shut, as does Arcane Lock. **Escape.** Climbing out needs a Climb Speed, climbing gear, or magic like Spider Climb. Cracks in the walls can make it easier. **Higher Levels.** Levels 5 to 10: 30 feet, 10 (3d6). Levels 11 to 16: 60 feet, 21 (6d6). Levels 17 to 20: 120 feet, 42 (12d6).",
"Icon of the Lower Aerial Kingdoms|VRGR": "A haunted trap covers a 10-foot-radius sphere around a 1-foot statue of a four-winged birdlike figure. Once per day, a creature entering hears wings and feels warm air. If still there at its next turn's start, it makes a DC 16 Wisdom save or is charmed and incapacitated for 1 minute, ending early if damaged or shaken by another's action. If charmed the full minute, magic jar applies, its soul entering the statue and a fiend's spirit taking its body. Dispel evil and good on the victim or destroying the statue ends this. The statue has AC 17, 15 hit points, and immunity to poison and psychic damage. Dispel evil and good on the statue permanently disarms the trap.",
"Morbid Memory|VRGR": "A mostly harmless haunted trap covers a room or 30-foot square and reveals the area's grim past. Entering brings faint whispers. If a creature is still there at the start of its next turn, an illusory scene of a terrible event plays for about 1 minute. Each creature that saw it makes a DC 10 Wisdom save or is frightened of the area for 1d4 rounds. Frightened creatures must Dash away by the safest route each turn if they can. The trap then stays dormant for 24 hours.",
"Net Trap|XGE": "Goblins prefer traps that leave intruders alive so they can be enslaved and put to work in mines or elsewhere.",
"Path of Blades|XGE": "A hidden tomb entrance in a buried pyramid, home of the Lost City of Cynidicea, is a hallway 20 feet wide and 160 feet long, riddled with traps and reached only through hidden secret doors. It is mostly clear, but from 80 feet to the 130-foot mark the floor is broken and difficult terrain.",
"Pit Trap|XGE": "A simple 10-foot-deep hole is hidden under canvas covered with leaves and dirt. It often blocks a monster lair's entrance and usually has narrow ledges along the sides for moving around it.",
"Pits|DMG": "**Simple.** Covered hole, usually 10 feet deep, DC 10 to spot, with depth-based fall damage. **Hidden.** DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) notes no foot traffic, and DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) confirms the cover. It swings open under a creature over a 10 or 20 foot pit. An iron spike or arcane lock keeps it shut. **Locking.** The spring cover snaps shut after a fall. DC 20 Strength pries it open. From inside, DC 15 Dexterity with thieves' tools disables the spring. **Spiked.** Spikes deal 11 (2d10) piercing plus fall damage. Poisoned spikes add a DC 13 Constitution save, taking 22 (4d10) poison damage on a failure or half on a success.",
"Poison Darts|DMG": "A hidden pressure plate fires poisoned darts from wall tubes hidden by dust, cobwebs, or art. Spotting the holes is DC 15. A DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check deduces the plate. Wedging an iron spike under the plate stops it. Stuffing the holes with cloth or wax stops the darts. More than 20 pounds on the plate releases four darts. Each makes a +8 ranged attack against a random target within 10 feet of the plate. A hit deals 2 (1d4) piercing damage, and the target makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 11 (2d10) poison damage on a failure or half on a success.",
"Poison Needle|DMG": "A needle hidden in a chest lock springs out 3 inches when opened without the right key. A creature in range takes 1 piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) poison damage and makes a DC 15 Constitution save or is poisoned for 1 hour. A DC 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check deduces the trap from lock alterations. A DC 15 Dexterity check with thieves' tools disarms it. Failing to pick the lock triggers it.",
"Poison Needle Trap|XGE": "A tiny poisoned needle hidden in a lock deters thieves. It usually guards a chest or the door to a treasure chamber.",
"Poisoned Darts|XDMG": "When a creature first moves onto the pressure plate on a turn, poisoned darts fire from wall tubes hidden by dust, cobwebs, or art. Each creature in their path makes a DC 13 Dexterity save or is hit by 1d3 darts, taking 3 (1d6) poison damage per dart. **Detect and Disarm.** A Search action and DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) finds the holes. Plugging them all stops the darts. The same check finds the plate. Wedging Iron Spikes under it stops the trigger. **Higher Levels.** Damage per dart is 7 (2d6) at levels 5 to 10, 14 (4d6) at levels 11 to 16, and 24 (7d6) at levels 17 to 20.",
"Poisoned Needle|XDMG": "A needle hidden in a lock stabs a creature that opens it with anything but the proper key. The creature makes a DC 11 Constitution save. On a failure it takes 5 (1d10) poison damage and is poisoned for 1 hour. On a success it takes half damage only. **Avoid.** Knock or similar magic does not trigger it. **Detect and Disarm.** A Search action and DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) finds the needle. An action and DC 15 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) disarms it, and failure triggers it. **Higher Levels.** Levels 5 to 10: 11 (2d10), DC 13. Levels 11 to 16: 22 (4d10), DC 15. Levels 17 to 20: 55 (10d10), DC 17.",
"Poisoned Tempest|XGE": "A yuan-ti temple trap meant to kill intruders. The room is 60 feet on a side with a 5-foot-wide stone door in the middle of each wall. A 10-foot coiled serpent statue stands in each corner, and each statue's eyes are rubies worth 200 gp apiece.",
"Rolling Sphere|DMG": "Over 20 pounds on a plate opens a ceiling trapdoor and frees a 10-foot stone sphere. DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) spots trapdoor and plate. DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) on the floor finds the plate, or on the ceiling the trapdoor. An iron spike under the plate stops it. All roll initiative, and the sphere has +8. It moves 60 feet straight, passing through spaces as difficult terrain. A creature it enters, or that enters it, makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or takes 55 (10d10) bludgeoning damage and falls prone. It stops at walls and cannot turn corners. An action and DC 20 Strength from within 5 feet cuts its speed by 15 feet. At 0 it stops.",
"Rolling Stone|XDMG": "A hidden plate releases a 5-foot-radius stone orb. It and nearby creatures roll Initiative, and it has +8. It moves 60 feet, turning off obstacles, passing through spaces as Difficult Terrain. When it first enters a creature's space on a turn, or a creature enters its space, that creature makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or takes 55 (10d10) bludgeoning damage and is Prone. It stops at walls. **Detect and Disarm.** Study and DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) deduces the plate. An Iron Spike under it stops it. **Destroy.** Large, AC 17, 100 HP, Damage Threshold 10, immune to poison and psychic. **Slow.** An action and DC 20 Strength (Athletics) cuts movement by 15 feet. At 0 it stops.",
"Scything Blade Trap|XGE": "Moving blades sweep through a chamber and threaten anyone nearby. A lever or similar simple device usually triggers it. Kobolds like it because it can take down bigger creatures.",
"Sleep of Ages Trap|XGE": "A pressure plate releases a spell that threatens to put intruders into deep slumber. The dungeon's guardians can then dispose of the sleepers more easily.",
"Sphere of Annihilation|DMG": "A stone face's 2-foot mouth holds magical darkness. It makes no sound, no light enters it, and any matter entering is obliterated. A DC 20 Intelligence (Arcana) check reveals a fixed sphere of annihilation that cannot be controlled or moved. Some versions enchant the face so chosen creatures feel compelled to crawl inside, like the sympathy aspect of antipathy/sympathy. A successful dispel magic (DC 18) removes that enchantment.",
"Sphere of Crushing Doom|XGE": "A court jester built this trap to protect his magic fool's cap. His tomb lies at the end of a 10-foot-wide, 150-foot-long hallway sloping steeply downward from north to south. The tomb's door is on the eastern wall at the bottom of the slope, at the south end.",
"Spiked Pit|XDMG": "A 10-foot-deep pit with a hinged lid has spikes at the bottom. A creature stepping on the lid falls in and the lid stays open. It takes 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) piercing damage. **Detect and Disarm.** Study and DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) finds the pit. An Iron Spike under the lid or Arcane Lock keeps it shut. **Escape.** Needs a Climb Speed, climbing gear, or magic like Spider Climb. **Higher Levels.** Levels 5 to 10: 30 feet, 10 (3d6) bludgeoning plus 13 (3d8) piercing. 11 to 16: 60 feet, 21 (6d6) plus 36 (8d8). 17 to 20: 120 feet, 42 (12d6) plus 57 (13d8).",
"Surface of the Sun|BMT": "Three 15 by 100 foot halls sit under a ceiling of scorching light. A gold key hangs in the right hall, a silver orb on a talon pedestal in the middle, and a skull door with a keyhole nose on the left. **Sun.** On initiative count 20 (losing ties), each creature takes 5 (1d10) radiant damage. **Talons.** Touching the orb snaps them shut: 11 (2d10) slashing damage and grappled (escape DC 15). AC 19, 10 hit points, immune to poison and psychic. DC 12 Wisdom (Perception) spots the plate. DC 13 Dexterity with thieves' tools opens them. **Key.** The 100-pound key becomes a flying sword a round after leaving its stand.",
"Test of the Empty Moon|BMT": "A square room has a silver bowl in the floor, ceiling sewer pipes, and a north portcullis under a moon glyph. A hidden scale under the bowl opens it. **Bowl.** 30 feet wide, 20 deep, 2,000 pounds, difficult terrain. Entering or ending a turn there needs a DC 15 Dexterity save or prone. Climbing out needs rope or magic. **Scale.** An Immovable Rod holds the bowl up and shows to Detect Magic. At 4,000 pounds the glyph is full and the portcullis opens. Shoving enemies in, Telekinesis, or Levitate adds weight. **Lever.** It drops the bowl, releases 1,000 pounds of water per minute, and frees four 500-pound Ochre Jelly. At 4 minutes flooding stops and the portcullis opens.",
"Arcane Effluence|NF": "Magical runoff creates a violet sludge with an acrid smell noticeable within 30 feet. A patch covers a 5-foot square. A creature touching it takes 3 (1d6) acid damage, and again at the start of each of its turns until the sludge is scraped off with an action or destroyed. Dispel Magic or a similar effect destroys it.",
"Avalanche|IDROTF": "These rules also cover rockslides. A typical avalanche is 300 feet wide, 150 long, and 30 thick. Nearby creatures roll initiative. On initiative counts 10 and 0, it travels 300 feet until it stops. Creatures in its space move with it, fall prone, and make a DC 15 Strength save, taking 1d10 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. When it stops, creatures are buried, blinded, restrained, and have Cover. They gain one exhaustion level per 5 minutes buried. An action and DC 15 Strength (Athletics) lets a creature dig free and end both conditions. Failing three times blocks further attempts. A creature neither restrained nor incapacitated can spend 1 minute freeing another.",
"Avalanche|TCE": "A typical avalanche or rockslide is 300 feet wide, 150 long, and 30 thick. Nearby creatures roll initiative. On initiative counts 10 and 0, it travels 300 feet until it stops. Creatures in its space move with it, fall prone, and make a DC 15 Strength save, taking 1d10 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. When it stops, creatures are buried, blinded, restrained, and have Cover. They gain 1 exhaustion level per 5 minutes buried. An action and DC 15 Strength (Athletics) lets a creature dig free and end both conditions. Failing three times blocks further attempts. A creature neither restrained nor incapacitated can spend 1 minute freeing another.",
"Blizzard|IDROTF": "A blizzard lasts 2d4 hours. Hearing range is 100 feet, ranged weapon attacks and hearing-based Wisdom (Perception) checks have disadvantage. Wind douses open flames, clears fog, erases tracks, and drops nonmagical flyers who cannot hover. Visibility is 30 feet, and without eye protection sight-based Wisdom (Perception) checks have disadvantage. Concentrating creatures make a DC 10 Constitution save at turn's end or lose it, unless sheltered. **Off Course.** A navigator makes a DC 15 Wisdom (Survival) check each hour. Failure makes no progress. Failing by 5 or more loses one untied member. Finding them takes a DC 15 Wisdom (Survival) group check each hour with no progress.",
"Brown Mold|DMG": "Brown mold drains warmth. A patch covers a 10-foot square, and within 30 feet it is frigid. A creature first moving within 5 feet on a turn or starting its turn there makes a DC 12 Constitution save, taking 22 (4d10) cold damage on a failure or half on a success. The mold is immune to fire. Fire within 5 feet makes it instantly spread a 10-foot square centered on the fire. Any cold damage effect destroys a patch instantly.",
"Brown Mold|XDMG": "Brown mold is a furry light-brown fungus that drains warmth. A patch covers a 10-foot square, and within 30 feet it is frigid. A creature first entering within 5 feet on a turn or starting its turn there makes a DC 12 Constitution save, taking 22 (4d10) cold damage on a failure or half on a success. It has immunity to fire damage. Fire within 5 feet makes it spread toward the fire as a new 10-foot-square patch. Any cold damage destroys a patch instantly.",
"Burning|XPHB": "A burning creature or object takes 1d4 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. As an action, you can put out flames on yourself by dropping Prone and rolling. Dousing, submerging, or suffocating the fire also puts it out.",
"Dead Magic Zone|XDMG": "A place where magic's fabric is torn. It works like the Antimagic Field spell but is permanent and usually no more than 300 feet across.",
"Deep Water|XDMG": "Water over 100 feet deep brings pressure and cold. After each hour swimming there, a creature without a Swim Speed makes a DC 10 Constitution save or gains 1 Exhaustion level.",
"Dehydration|XPHB": "A creature needs daily water by size. A creature drinking under half the amount gains 1 Exhaustion level at day's end. That exhaustion cannot be removed until it drinks the full daily amount. Daily needs: Tiny 1/4 gallon, Small 1 gallon, Medium 1 gallon, Large 4 gallons, Huge 16 gallons, Gargantuan 64 gallons.",
"Demon Ichor|BGDIA": "Ichor from dead demons pools in Avernus. On direct contact there, a creature makes a DC 10 Constitution save. Fiends, oozes, plants, and undead succeed automatically. Failure rolls Flesh Warping. Remove curse ends it all. **Coated Weapons.** Damage from an ichor-coated weapon forces the same save, then the coating is gone. **d100.** 01-05 odd colors. 06-10 eyestalks. 11-15 claws. 16-20 speed -10. 21-25 15-foot dim cone. 26-30 fly 30. 31-35 deafened. 36-40 tusks. 41-45 +1 AC, Charisma -2. 46-50 crawl only. 51-55 reach +5. 56-60 speed +10. 61-65 tail. 66-70 darkvision 120. 71-75 triple weight. 76-80 half weight. 81-85 big head. 86-90 fly 5. 91-95 vulnerable to bludgeoning, piercing, slashing. 96-00 advantage on saves against charmed, frightened, stunned.",
"Desecrated Ground|DMG": "Ancient evil can taint cemeteries and catacombs. The area can be any size, and detect evil and good reveals it. Undead standing on it have advantage on all saving throws. A flask of holy water purifies a 10-foot square, and hallow purifies the ground in its area.",
"Extreme Cold|DMG": "At 0 degrees Fahrenheit or below, an exposed creature makes a DC 10 Constitution save at the end of each hour or gains one exhaustion level. Creatures with resistance or immunity to cold damage succeed automatically, as do those in cold weather gear or adapted to cold climates.",
"Extreme Cold|XDMG": "At 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower, an exposed creature makes a DC 10 Constitution save at the end of each hour or gains 1 Exhaustion level. Creatures with Resistance or Immunity to Cold damage succeed automatically.",
"Bile Lichen|FRAIF": "A toxic green-yellow lichen grows where heat and cold mix. A patch covers a 5-foot square. Touching it releases spores in a 10-foot Cube that lasts 1d4 hours. A creature first entering the cloud on a turn or starting its turn there makes a DC 14 Constitution save, taking 11 (2d10) poison damage and contracting Lichen Plague on a failure, or half damage only on a success.",
"Calim Sandstorm|FRAIF": "A Calim sandstorm is at least 300 feet across and lasts 1d6 hours. Its area is Heavily Obscured and open flames go out. After each hour inside, a creature makes a DC 10 Constitution save or gains 1 Exhaustion level.",
}
